    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21241" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hȳsōpum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hysso-</span></b> ), i,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕσσωπος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>hyssop</i>: Hyssopus
			officinalis, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 25, 11, 87, § 136</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">26, 11, 70, §
				114</span></i>; <i><span class="en">26, 12,
				76, § 124</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">asperges me hyssopo, et mundabor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Psa. 50, 8 al.</span></i>
			—And in a form corresp. to the Gr., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hyssōpus</span></b> ,
			i, f., <i><span class="en">Cels. 4,
			8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 7, 5 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—Also scanned
			hȳsŏpum, Aemil. Mac. de Hyssopo.</div>
